id: pm-erogk1
title: Refuse local package installation when source scan stops at entry limit
description: "GitHub #1321: local package source inspection reaches max_entries=10000, reports copy.complete=false and stop_reason=entry_limit, yet dry-run and real install return ok=true, warnings=[] and exit 0; real path may activate a partial package. Fail closed before write/activation, give a packed-package recovery hint, and align dry-run readiness."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-27T00:37:15.358Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-27T08:49:14.564Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-27T08:36:28.474Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-27T08:36:28.474Z"
author: "harness:codex"
parent: pm-x6jf
resolution: "The SDK install planner now rejects entry- or depth-limited directory scans with a stable refusal code and actionable archive recovery; generated SDK contracts, tests and docs include the new behavior."
expected_result: Dry and real package installs never accept a truncated local source scan or create a partial package; packed archives remain installable.
actual_result: "Focused linked test passed, isolated manual project refused SDK and CLI truncated scans without destination writes and installed/activated the packed archive; full coverage was 100/100/100/100 and packed npm/Bun smoke passed. Local timing gates showed host-sensitive overages; hosted CI is pending."
